On Wed, 2014-02-19 at 15:35 +0700, uvan@apm.com wrote:
> Dear all,
>  
> I’m trying to used Linaro toolchain to build Aarch64 images, but this
> toolchain require all libraries must be deployed
> under /lib/<arch-linux-gnu>, /usr/lib/<arch-linux-gnu>.
>  
> I already made external-linaro-toolchain.bb to install all toolchain’s
> libraries in corrected location(meant under /lib/<arch-linux-gnu>
> and /usr/lib/<arch-linux-gnu>, but other libraries generated by Yocto
> right now will install to default location is /lib and /usr/lib.
>  
> Do we have any way to ask Yocto generate libraries
> to /usr/lib/<arch-linux-gnu> ?

Change the values of libdir and base_libdir?

That isn't tested or supported but in theory should work. Reality is you
may run into some issues you may need to fix but there shouldn't be too
many of them as we so test changing libdir to /usr/lib64 and so on.

Cheers,

